<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7687" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναύδ-ητος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναύδ-ᾱτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not
				to be spoken, unutterable</i>: hence, <i>horrible,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναυδάτῳ μένει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					897
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄφατον ἀναύδητον λόγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					783
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>unspoken, impossible,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδὲν ἀναύδατον φατίσαιμ᾽ ἄν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					715
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>speechless,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				968
			</span></i> (cj.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
